		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=17&amp;p=304#p304"><![CDATA[
Its on the To Do list to make this as flexible as the old hotpot mode, but I changed the way the power is handled in the Tier 2 version to be in steps and it was easier for me to get the hotspot working,  to just calculate out the approximate step for each % power setting<br><br>The problem is really that the power curve is only relatively linear between 1W and 5W.<br><br>Below 1W the power curve is exponential.<br><br>To get the 250, 500 and 750mW settings relatively accurate, I subtract fixed values below the calibration PA drive value for 1W (where the raw value is normally around 1600 )<br><br>If someone could work out an equation of % power -&gt; PA drive value, it would be great , as we could use it for the hotspot<br><br>BTW. I did consider adding some more power options e.g 50mW and also 5W+  (i.e drive the PA to the Max)<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Tue Nov 19, 2019 10:46 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
